# Milestone: M3
# Covers: memory-leak regression for 'at (e?)' watchers holding a reference
#         on their creator object; Foo instances created in a loop should be
#         collectible after the loop (no hidden watcher root).
# blocked: requires System.memCheck() + Event type + at(e?) (System not implemented)
# matrix-row: stdlib-system
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture creates a Foo class with an Event slot and an 'at (e?)' watcher
#   in its init(), then checks for leaks via System.memCheck().  This requires:
#   (1) class definition with init() (M4), (2) Event.new() type (M6 stdlib),
#   (3) 'at (e?)' reactive watcher (M5 reactive runtime), (4) System.memCheck()
#   (M6 stdlib).  The underlying GC root walker for watchers is implemented at
#   M3 (T36) but the urbiscript-level Event/at-watcher surface is M5/M6.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Event type and reactive runtime):
# # import System.*;
# # var Global.nb_iter = 500 | System.systemFiles = []|;
# # { class Foo { var e = Event.new(); function init() { at(e?) echo(1) } };
# #   System.memCheck(closure() { for(Global.nb_iter) { Foo.new() } }); }|;
